        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8c8fd4d8-3998-54bc-8030-2ae19ab16669",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Smylie, Liz Smylie, Elizabeth Sayers, Vasek Pospisil, Jack Sock, Nicole Provis, Jo-Anne Faull, Julie Richardson\n- Events: 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles, 2014 Wimbledon Championships, 2015 Indian Wells Masters\n- Topics: Professional tennis, Grand Slam titles, women's doubles, mixed doubles\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth Smylie, née Sayers and sometimes known as Liz Smylie, was born on 11 April 1963 and is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\n- Elizabeth Smylie won four Grand Slam titles during her career, including one in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\n- In the 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles, defending champions Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie lost in the quarterfinals to Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Jack Sock won the men's doubles title at the 2014 Wimbledon Championships.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Jack Sock won the men's doubles title at the 2015 Indian Wells Masters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
